## Findings

### From digest/EVENTS.md (key)
- No world-event object anywhere. Nearest: conformance ACT- {id?,description,actor{role,body},at|period,evidence}, lives only inside determination (conformance l.19, K171); no act w/o determination, no act-act relations, one actor, no uncertain date.
- progressions (L5, built): declared flow vs observed flow (D-128), document-threaded; missing_predecessor, overdue_successor, cardinality_exceeded; out-of-order NOT built (needs placed doc's own date; Framework 8.2 src 965-968); overdue anchored on reading.at=retrieval (progressions index 860-897, K1444(ii) corrects, unbuilt); calendar days only. Fork/merge graph gap (Framework §11 1707-1710).
- meeting-calendar.mjs:148 emits meeting refs {body,date,status scheduled|cancelled|rescheduled, agenda, minutes}; meeting-minutes.mjs:384-418 item outcome/result/vote tallies; unqueryable as events. calendar compare() no caller in plane (DP l.11,372).
- docprofile event/notice/routine significance = document-change "event" (clash). Also "event" in tasks R1, wizard-scripts R15, queue R32 DEC-16 "event is unit of state".
- filings R9 chronology: only assembled timeline; per packet; from act, publication ratified_at, action state history, correspondence, clock; UTC day; ties by source id; undated listed apart (filings index.mjs:1020-1046).
- actions correspondence ledger + D-147 lifecycle (stage, follows, outcome, due_by, due_cite); responds_to edge; requestLifecycleOf passed_unanswered.
- jurisdictions R26 deadlines starts ∈ received|filed|act|known; R7 practice.minutes_due_days UNMEASURED; R41 time_zone, hours; R33 holidays.
- standards R6 supersedes (one successor), R7 inForce, R8 standardsIn({at}).
- consequences R5 causation inquiry -> established|unproven; DEC-14 sequence≠cause; DEC-84(10) cause member-authored, conformance R22 cause {statement,evidence}.
- DEC-60/IS §5,§16: typed support/undercut/rebuttal withdrawn "roles are not types"; record does not compute over claim relations. Must distinguish event-event relations (world facts, sourced) from evidence roles.
- SR §5.1 closed edge vocab: cites, relates_to, elevated_into, initiates, derived_from, supersedes, corroborates; responds_to/references/action_basis outside it.
- Intake §3a corroboration edge between independent records of same fact (event identity across sources hook).
- Six deadline designs no relation (INVENTORY §3 l.35).
- One DO alarm with consumer registry (15 consumers); no cron.
- Framework §9.1: "keeping a timeline of what happened when" partly; nothing assembles them. Content types overlap: minutes = record+attendance+votes.
- Publication D-543/D-573/review R17: order within same second undetermined. CPR §5 timeline form: stated-date order, undated placed nowhere & counted.
- Retrieval: no event-date field; query-language FIELDS time only record times. 22ms metadata+time range at 20k.
- MK §2 / provenance R28 observed_at date or UTC instant, no approx.
- U41 HANDOFF Time: days UTC, tz unused, no recurring-meeting model, no effective dates extracted, chronology only in counsel packet. Courts: no case tracking.
- DEC-10 overdue relevance filter: connected to focus/project; notify once.
- K1447: occurrence of a sourced duty may become a leg (stage 2), not yet in inquiry R4.
- Bob's contract case (IS §5, DEC-60): "emergency declared two weeks after contract signed" — order carries meaning.
- ACTION-PLAN worked example: certification + deposit = two government acts, dependent.
- Founding case: transfers FY2012-21, audit Feb 2022, recs deadline Oct 2023, label discontinued between FY21-FY24 (uncertain date); CPRA 26-3028 non-response.
- corpus-export lacks progression_* tables (M5 verification).
- temporal-expectation-due catalogued no producer (queuestate.mjs:164).
